---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# session_title_writers: who writes a session's name, and how every page
# that shows it stays right (go/tests/model/README.md). The history half
# (the live small model, `bough summarize`, shutdown naming, the file's
# writers) is specs/session_title_history.fizz: together they were far
# past the state budget, and they meet only at history's title, which
# here is one step (AutoTitle).
#
# Checked against:
#   serve  internal/serve/api.go rename -> metaVerb -> Supervisor.SetTitle
#          (supervisor.go), which saves meta.json before it answers and
#          rolls memory back when the save fails; rowOf (api.go) names the
#          row meta.Title when non-empty, else history's title.
#   page   web/src/app.tsx: refresh (the list read: polls every 4 s, 12 s
#          with a session open; readSeq drops an answer when a later read
#          started), the `selected` effect (the opening lookup and every
#          event's catchUp, GET /api/sessions/{id}, merge r.session into
#          rows), onRename (POST, then an awaited refresh, then the dialog
#          closes); the sidebar row, the thread <h1> and document.title
#          all read that one row through sessionTitle (render.tsx:
#          plainTitle(title) || summary || "Untitled · <date>").
#          web/src/dialog.tsx: submit trims, textBlocked refuses the text
#          it opened with unless empty.
#
# The spec says what the design must be; where the code today differs it
# says so under DIVERGES, and the model tests of this flow are where the
# difference turns red:
#
# DIVERGES 1 (stale catch-up). A catchUp or the opening lookup that
#   started before a rename was acknowledged still lands after it and
#   replaces the row with the old name: header, sidebar and tab revert
#   until the next poll (12 s). Only refresh's own list reads carry
#   readSeq. The spec drops every read that started before the ack
#   (Rename's inflight = "none"); the code does that for polls only.
# DIVERGES 2 (blank titles). SetTitle stores meta.Title untrimmed. The
#   page trims before it posts, but any other client (curl, a second
#   page's API) can store "   ": rowOf then prefers it to history's title
#   (non-empty), and every page shows "Untitled" (or the summary). The
#   spec's server trims: RenameBlank hands the name back to history.
#
# Corrections to the mapped model:
# - sidebar, header and tab read one row (`row` is rows.find(...), the
#   sidebar maps rows, the tab is sessionTitle(row)), so a catch-up merge
#   moves all three at once and they never disagree; the invariant stays
#   as the claim the browser test checks.
# - "restart_during_save" is not one state but two outcomes: serve dies
#   after SetTitle saved (the rename survives but the page never hears the
#   answer and shows the error) or before (nothing changed). Neither
#   breaks an acknowledged rename: SetTitle saves before it answers.
# - "textBlocked stops pinning the provisional title" is real but not a
#   safety property: the dialog refuses the text it opened with, which is
#   the SHOWN name, not meta. With meta empty and the opening line shown,
#   typing that line again is refused, so a person cannot keep the
#   opening line as the name once the small model renames it (they must
#   type a variation). Not modelled (it would add a meta value per history
#   name); reported with the other findings.
#
# Values. Names: "prompt" the opening line (provisional), "auto" the small
# model's final name, "mine" typed in this tab, "theirs" typed in another
# tab, "blank" a whitespace-only title. What a page shows: the name, or
# "untitled" for an empty or blank title. The session starts prompted: a
# session with no name at all has nothing a blank title could hide.
#
# Fields:
#   hist     history's title: "prompt" until the small model's "auto"
#   meta     serve's meta.Title in memory
#   saved    meta.Title in meta.json: what a restart reads back
#   title    the row's title as GET /api/sessions answers it
#   sidebar, header, tab
#            this tab's list row, thread <h1> and document.title
#   inflight the title a read this tab started saw ("none": no read out).
#            One read stands for the list poll and the thread's catchUp
#            (an event, the title event among them, arms one).
#   acked    this tab's last rename was acknowledged and nothing has
#            renamed the session since
#   dialog   "closed", "open", "saving" (POST out), "failed" (error shown)
#   typed    the text a saving dialog posted ("" hands the name back)
#   other    what a second tab on the same session shows

# What a page shows for a row title.
def shown(t):
    if t == "" or t == "blank":
        return "untitled"
    return t

def rowtitle(meta, hist):
    if meta != "":
        return meta
    return hist

role Session:
    action Init:
        self.hist = "prompt"
        self.meta = ""
        self.saved = ""
        self.title = "prompt"
        self.sidebar = "prompt"
        self.header = "prompt"
        self.tab = "prompt"
        self.inflight = "none"
        self.acked = False
        self.dialog = "closed"
        self.typed = ""
        self.other = "prompt"

    # The small model's one final name lands in history (the history half
    # is session_title_history.fizz); serve's row changes only when no
    # rename hides it. Its "title" event arms this tab's catch-up, which
    # is ReadStart.
    atomic action AutoTitle:
        require self.hist == "prompt"
        self.hist = "auto"
        t = rowtitle(self.meta, self.hist)
        if t != self.title:
            self.acked = False
        self.title = t

    # A list poll or an event's catchUp leaves: it reads the row as it is
    # now. Fair: the poll runs for as long as the page is open. Only a
    # read that could change something is modelled.
    atomic fair<strong> action ReadStart:
        require self.inflight == "none"
        s = shown(self.title)
        require self.header != s
        self.inflight = self.title

    # Its answer lands and replaces the row: all three surfaces move.
    atomic fair<strong> action ReadLand:
        require self.inflight != "none"
        s = shown(self.inflight)
        self.sidebar = s
        self.header = s
        self.tab = s
        self.inflight = "none"

    # Settings > Rename…, prefilled with the header's name.
    atomic action OpenRename:
        require self.dialog == "closed"
        self.dialog = "open"

    # Rename pressed: the POST leaves. textBlocked refuses the text the
    # dialog opened with (the header then) unless it is empty; nothing
    # but this tab's own rename makes the header "mine".
    atomic action Submit:
        require self.dialog in ["open", "failed"]
        text = any ["", "mine"]
        require text == "" or text != self.header
        self.typed = text
        self.dialog = "saving"

    # SetTitle saved meta.json and answered; onRename's awaited refresh
    # lands and the dialog closes on the new name. Every read that
    # started before the ack is dropped (DIVERGES 1: the code drops only
    # its own polls).
    atomic fair<strong> action SaveLands:
        require self.dialog == "saving"
        self.meta = self.typed
        self.saved = self.typed
        self.title = rowtitle(self.meta, self.hist)
        s = shown(self.title)
        self.sidebar = s
        self.header = s
        self.tab = s
        self.inflight = "none"
        self.acked = True
        self.dialog = "closed"
        self.typed = ""

    # The save failed (disk full, 404): SetTitle rolled memory back, the
    # dialog shows the error and stays up.
    atomic action SaveFails:
        require self.dialog == "saving"
        self.dialog = "failed"
        self.typed = ""

    atomic action Dismiss:
        require self.dialog in ["open", "failed"]
        self.dialog = "closed"

    # A second tab renames the same session (its own dialog, not
    # modelled). This tab learns it only from a read.
    atomic action RenameElsewhere:
        require self.meta != "theirs"
        self.meta = "theirs"
        self.saved = "theirs"
        self.title = rowtitle(self.meta, self.hist)
        self.acked = False
        self.other = shown(self.title)

    # Another client posts a whitespace-only title. The server trims it:
    # a blank name hands the name back to history (DIVERGES 2: the code
    # stores it and every page says Untitled).
    atomic action RenameBlank:
        require self.meta != ""
        self.meta = ""
        self.saved = ""
        self.title = rowtitle(self.meta, self.hist)
        self.acked = False

    # serve restarts (update, crash, kickstart): meta comes back from
    # meta.json. A read out when it died fails. A POST out when it died
    # either saved first (the name changed, but the page never heard the
    # answer) or did not; either way the dialog shows an error.
    atomic action ServeRestart:
        if self.dialog == "saving":
            landed = any [True, False]
            if landed:
                self.meta = self.typed
                self.saved = self.typed
            self.dialog = "failed"
            self.typed = ""
        self.meta = self.saved
        t = rowtitle(self.meta, self.hist)
        if t != self.title:
            self.acked = False
        self.title = t
        self.inflight = "none"

    # The second tab's own poll.
    atomic fair<strong> action PollOther:
        s = shown(self.title)
        require self.other != s
        self.other = s

action Init:
    session = Session()

# After this tab's rename is acknowledged, and until something renames the
# session again, no read that started earlier changes the name back.
always assertion AckedRenameSticks:
    if not session.acked:
        return True
    return session.header == shown(session.title)

# The list row, the thread header and the tab never disagree, through
# catch-up merges and polls alike.
always assertion OneTitleEverywhere:
    return session.sidebar == session.header and session.header == session.tab

# A blank title never hides history's: the row always has a name.
always assertion BlankNeverHidesHistory:
    return shown(session.title) != "untitled"

# What serve holds in memory is what meta.json holds: a rename that was
# acknowledged (or that saved before serve died) survives a restart, and
# a failed save changes nothing a restart would take back.
always assertion RenameSurvivesRestart:
    return session.meta == session.saved and session.title == rowtitle(session.meta, session.hist)

# Every tab ends up showing the session's current name.
always eventually assertion EveryTabCatchesUp:
    s = shown(session.title)
    return session.header == s and session.other == s
